From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 06:49:47 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 23/23] tools(pad): say how many presses UN5_PAD_SCRIPT holds

A script that parsed to nothing (zsh reads "$t:start" as a history
modifier and drops the button) failed silently.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 ps2xRuntime/src/lib/Kernel/Stubs/Pad.cpp | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/Kernel/Stubs/Pad.cpp b/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/Kernel/Stubs/Pad.cpp
index 6c42cf0..21dcf17 100644
--- a/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/Kernel/Stubs/Pad.cpp
+++ b/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/Kernel/Stubs/Pad.cpp
@@ -332,6 +332,9 @@ namespace ps2_stubs
                         press.mask = static_cast<uint16_t>(press.mask | scriptButtonMask(name));
                     script.push_back(press);
                 }
+                if (!script.empty())
+                    std::cerr << "[pad:script] " << script.size() << " presses, first at " << script.front().tick
+                              << ", last at " << script.back().tick << std::endl;
                 return script;
             }();
             return s_script;
